AIM
To design and develop an interactive real estate website using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript that allows users to search for houses and lands based on location, property type, and budget.
ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Create an HTML page containing a property search form and property listings.
3. Apply CSS to design an attractive and responsive user interface.
4. Use JavaScript to filter properties based on location, property type, and maximum budget.
5. Display the matching properties and their details.
6. Display a message when no matching properties are found.
7. Stop the program.
HTML CODE — index.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Home Finder</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Home Finder</h1>
        <p>Find your perfect home within your budget</p>
    </header>

    <main>
        <section class="search">
            <h2>Search Properties</h2>
            <input type="text" id="location" placeholder="Enter location">

            <select id="type">
                <option value="all">All Properties</option>
                <option value="House">House</option>
                <option value="Land">Land</option>
                <option value="Apartment">Apartment</option>
            </select>

            <input type="number" id="budget"
                   placeholder="Maximum budget (₹)">

            <button onclick="searchProperties()">Search</button>
        </section>

        <h2>Available Properties</h2>
        <div id="properties" class="property-list"></div>
        <p id="message"></p>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 Home Finder</p>
    </footer>

    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

CSS CODE — style.css
body {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background: #f2f5f9;
